{"availability":"available","full":"mkbhardwas12/purposemesh","name":"purposemesh","description":"Purpose-bound authorization reference: RBAC + ABAC + ReBAC, row/field controls, fidelity gates, lifecycle governance, and a tested 100K synthetic-data path.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":163,"forks":46,"created":"2026-08-17T02:04:29Z","updated":"2026-10-13T17:01:22Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://mkbhardwas12.github.io/purposemesh/","topics":["abac","access-control","authorization","authzen","data-governance","least-privilege","policy-as-code","purpose-bound-access","purposemesh","rbac","rebac","typescript","zero-trust"],"demo":"https://mkbhardwas12.github.io/purposemesh/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T02:58:31.617Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T02:58:31.617Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T02:58:31.617Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T04:29:54.895Z","stars":163,"forks":46},{"at":"2026-10-17T02:58:31.617Z","stars":163,"forks":46}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Implemented today in the local React/Fastify/PDP/SQLite path; external enforcement requires a conformant adapter with published, target-version-scoped passing evidence, target apply, and verified read-back.","PurposeMesh is an open-source Technical Preview for authorization enforcement assurance across shared data. It combines a small RBAC capability vocabulary with ABAC scope and ReBAC relationships, then returns server-enforced row, field, purpose, classification, and lifecycle obligations.","Its core policy envelope is a Contract Capsule: one reviewable unit that keeps action, data scope, fields, purpose, conditions, approvals, and expiry together as policy moves across applications and platforms."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mkbhardwas12/purposemesh/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"653fd8f17eb1cf6fb70c623b8b65ca9c5b44fba1de2927fb84409dfaaea892f8","extractedAt